From 45dcf1b530c6e065b4caf496ddd9399bc102d7ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 21:45:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 098/145] media: meson: vdec: vp9: do not touch the workspace
 after freeing it

codec_vp9_stop() frees the workspace but leaves vp9->workspace_vaddr
pointing at it.  codec_vp9_threaded_isr() reads that workspace in four
places - the adaptive-probability blocks, and codec_vp9_fetch_rpm(),
which walks RPM_BUF_SIZE u16s out of it.  Both take vp9->lock, so an
interrupt already blocked on the lock when the session is torn down
proceeds the moment stop() releases it, and reads memory that
dma_free_coherent() has just unmapped.

On a VIM3 (G12B) that is a hard oops in the interrupt thread:

  Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address ffff80008f138806
  FSC = 0x07: level 3 translation fault
  CPU: 0 PID: 507 Comm: irq/33-vdec
  pc : codec_vp9_threaded_isr+0x12c/0xddc [meson_vdec]
  Call trace:
   codec_vp9_threaded_isr+0x12c/0xddc [meson_vdec]
   vdec_threaded_isr+0x1c/0x24 [meson_vdec]
   irq_thread_fn+0x24/0xa0
  genirq: exiting task "irq/33-vdec" (507) is an active IRQ thread (irq 33)

The faulting instruction is the ldrh in codec_vp9_fetch_rpm() and the
address is the freed coherent mapping.

The last line is what makes this more than a splat: the threaded handler
for irq 33 is gone.  The machine stays up and /dev/video0 still opens,
but no decode completion is ever processed again - every later session,
in any codec, streams on and returns zero frames until the box is
rebooted.  It presents as "the decoder stopped working", nothing points
at VP9, and the oops may already have scrolled away.

Reached by ending a VP9 session while a decode interrupt is outstanding,
which is what a player does on stop, on a seek, and on any abnormal exit.

Clear the pointer under the lock and have the interrupt handler give up
when the workspace has gone.

Fixes: 00c43088aa68 ("media: meson: vdec: add VP9 decoder support")
Signed-off-by: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
---
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_vp9.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_vp9.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_vp9.c
index b0c3fea107d3..fdf77b060e7e 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_vp9.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_vp9.c
@@ -847,10 +847,12 @@ static int codec_vp9_stop(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 	struct codec_vp9 *vp9 = sess->priv;
 
 	mutex_lock(&vp9->lock);
-	if (vp9->workspace_vaddr)
+	if (vp9->workspace_vaddr) {
 		dma_free_coherent(core->dev, SIZE_WORKSPACE,
 				  vp9->workspace_vaddr,
 				  vp9->workspace_paddr);
+		vp9->workspace_vaddr = NULL;
+	}
 
 	codec_hevc_free_fbc_buffers(sess, &vp9->common);
 	mutex_unlock(&vp9->lock);
@@ -2123,6 +2125,14 @@ static irqreturn_t codec_vp9_threaded_isr(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 
 	mutex_lock(&vp9->lock);
+	if (!vp9->workspace_vaddr) {
+		/*
+		 * codec_vp9_stop() ran while this interrupt was in flight and
+		 * took the lock first.  Everything below reads the workspace.
+		 */
+		goto unlock;
+	}
+
 	if (dec_status != VP9_HEAD_PARSER_DONE) {
 		dev_err(core->dev_dec, "Unrecognized dec_status: %08X\n",
 			dec_status);
-- 
2.43.0

